 "structural_change": "HBM-WBK8 10-20 census-safe successor of hbm_wbk_q2_1020 (q2 mapped native census FAIL 2,219 drivers >32, max 232: a PC's combinational pop drove nine 32-b FIFOs + skid; 32-b ot_link_afifo AW3/RCOPY4 read copies 65 loads, entry enables 56; w_k_rdy 39-49; payload SRAM rows at 41.04 pitch off the 43.2 lattice). New core ot_hbm_svc_wb_kq8_core: 16-b reviewed ot_link_afifo AW2 RCOPY3 in ping-pong pairs (8 entries/PC as q2), lockstep REGISTERED per-slice pop copies, 3-entry one-hot K pin rings (w_k_v a flop, w_k_rdy one AND per slice), 16-b select/enable copies, 3-level reset relays; SRAM rows re-pitched to 43.2 (y=86.4+43.2k).",
 "slot_change_request": "d4g wbk_<q> x4: new slot 777.6 x 518.4 (pin-bound: N = 16 K ports 4,626 pins at 5.95/um toward the quadrant's 4 vmks leaves; S = DMA wd 2,312 + stream control at 3.2/um toward hb_dbk_<q>); 32 payload SRAMs as 4 abutted 8-high columns (one per stream_fifo_clk root) on the 43.2 lattice",
